  "body": "- [ ] I, the PR author, have personally reviewed every line of this PR.\n\n## What does this PR do?\n\nKeep pure evaluation out of the MFSDP v2 training execution order and prefetch cursor. An `eval()` forward under `no_grad()` has no corresponding backward event; recording or consuming it as training can invalidate the next training forward/backward order. Training-mode `no_grad()` forwards retain their existing recomputation behavior.\n\n## Validation\n\nOn this independent branch, five distributed cases pass on each of two RTX PRO 6000 GPUs. They cover evaluation before the first recorded training step, train/eval/train, grouped and sequential MoE experts, unchanged evaluation parameters and Adam state, and an unchanged execution order and cursor.\n\nSource: [4110362](https://github.com/WEIXILIN0307/Megatron-LM/commit/41103622852c379074ad993cf592fb799df65a21), based on `a7a6d2225`. Commands, per-rank logs and source checksums: https://github.com/WEIXILIN0307/Megatron-LM/tree/c9d6469a76afdcf36e5428cc826cae4b708af15b/mfsdp-v2-core-split-20261112. Full upstream CI has not been run.\n\n## Issue tracking\n\nPrerequisite for #9112; design context: #9113. This fix is independent of CUDA graphs.\n\n## Code provenance\n\nNo code copied or adapted from external repositories.\n\n## Contribution process\n\n- [x] Relevant unit tests accompany the fix.\n- [ ] Registered functional-test coverage added.\n- [x] Formatter and lint pipeline checked against the already-fetched base.\n- No numerical GPU kernel changes; determinism coverage check is not applicable.\n",
